    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "formulas_reference",
      "content": "## Key Formulas\n\n### Power and Torque Relationship\n**P = T × ω** where:\n- P = power (W)\n- T = torque (Nm)\n- ω = angular velocity (rad/s)\n\n### Alternative Forms\n**P = T × 2π × nrps** (using rotations per second)\n\n**P = T × π × nrpm / 30** (using rotations per minute)\n\n**P = T × nrpm / 5252** (imperial units: power in hp, torque in ft lbf)\n\n### Rearranged for Torque\n**T = 30 × P / (π × nrpm)**\n\n### Angular Acceleration Torque\n**T = I × α** where:\n- I = moment of inertia (kg⋅m²)\n- α = angular acceleration (rad/s²)\n\n### Unit Conversions\n- 1 radian = 360° / 2π ≈ 57.296°\n- Angular velocity: ω = 2π × rpm / 60"
    }
